WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:14.034
The third graders were restless.

2
00:00:14.035 --> 00:00:18.961
They wanted to be playing outdoors, not sitting in the classroom.

3
00:00:18.962 --> 00:00:21.736
Mr. Higgins stood in front of the class.

4
00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:25.323
"What happens in spring?" he asked.

5
00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:30.089
"We plan for summer vacation!" said Katie.

6
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.698
"True," said Mr. Higgins.

7
00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.013
"But it's not time for that yet, Katie.

8
00:00:35.014 --> 00:00:37.385
Who has another answer?"

9
00:00:37.386 --> 00:00:40.931
"Flowers bloom!" said Laura.

10
00:00:40.932 --> 00:00:44.854
"Birds build nests!" said Joy.

11
00:00:44.855 --> 00:00:49.536
"Good," said Mr. Higgins. "What about the weather?"

12
00:00:49.537 --> 00:00:55.927
"Sunny and warm," Katie said, looking out the window with longing.

13
00:00:55.928 --> 00:01:00.510
"But sometimes it can be stormy," said Luke.

14
00:01:00.511 --> 00:01:04.002
"Twisters!" said Carlos Ramirez.

15
00:01:04.003 --> 00:01:07.323
He lived two houses down from Luke.

16
00:01:07.324 --> 00:01:10.059
"That's right," said Mr. Higgins.

17
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.014
"Twisters, or tornadoes, often strike in the spring.

18
00:01:14.015 --> 00:01:17.695
Who can explain what a tornado is?"

19
00:01:17.696 --> 00:01:19.708
Carlos spoke up again.

20
00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:23.502
"It's a strong wind that spins around and around.

21
00:01:23.503 --> 00:01:28.796
It's shaped like a funnel, and it hangs down from a storm cloud.

22
00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:32.246
A tornado can carry off a cow or a school bus.

23
00:01:32.247 --> 00:01:35.958
It can even lift a house up in the air!"

24
00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:41.003
"Tornadoes are very dangerous," agreed Mr. Higgins.

25
00:01:41.004 --> 00:01:43.707
"That's why every spring we prepare.

26
00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:47.483
We practice what to do if a tornado comes."

27
00:01:47.484 --> 00:01:52.247
"Are we going to have a tornado drill?" Katie asked hopefully.

28
00:01:52.248 --> 00:01:55.750
"Yes, Katie. Later," said Mr. Higgins.

29
00:01:55.751 --> 00:02:00.278
"Now who remembers what the tornado alarm sounds like?"

30
00:02:00.279 --> 00:02:04.794
"Three siren blasts!" said Luke.

31
00:02:04.795 --> 00:02:07.524
"Yes," said Mr. Higgins.

32
00:02:07.525 --> 00:02:12.079
"Then we all get in line, and I lead the way to the basement."

33
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.203
"And when we get there, we take cover!" said Katie.

34
00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:19.973
"HA! That's the best part!"

35
00:02:19.974 --> 00:02:23.056
"Thank you, Katie," said Mr. Higgins.

36
00:02:23.057 --> 00:02:27.250
"Now who wants to demonstrate the take-cover position?"

37
00:02:27.251 --> 00:02:30.477
"I do!" cried Katie.

38
00:02:30.478 --> 00:02:35.104
"Please settle down, Katie," said Mr. Higgins, frowning a little.

39
00:02:35.105 --> 00:02:38.653
"Carlos, why don't you show us?"

40
00:02:38.654 --> 00:02:41.218
Carlos walked to the front of the class.

41
00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:46.133
He knelt on the floor and put his arms and hands over his head.

42
00:02:46.134 --> 00:02:49.379
"Perfect!" said Mr. Higgins.

43
00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.554
The third graders cheered.

44
00:02:51.555 --> 00:02:55.492
Carlos grinned and returned to his desk.

45
00:02:55.493 --> 00:02:58.951
"We're ready for the drill!" said Mr. Higgins.

46
00:02:58.952 --> 00:03:01.608
"Now get out your math homework."

47
00:03:01.609 --> 00:03:04.327
Everybody groaned.

48
00:03:04.328 --> 00:03:08.077
After math came social studies and then lunch.

49
00:03:08.078 --> 00:03:13.580
When the children returned from the lunchroom, it was time for art.

50
00:03:13.581 --> 00:03:17.650
"Let's work on our tornado posters," announced Mr. Higgins.

51
00:03:17.651 --> 00:03:21.247
"Katie, please pass out the magic markers."

52
00:03:21.248 --> 00:03:29.394
Katie grabbed the coffee can filled with markers when suddenly—weeee-uuuuu, weeee-uuuuu, weeee-uuuuu.

53
00:03:29.395 --> 00:03:33.856
Katie jumped and the markers flew into the air.

54
00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:37.609
"Tornado drill!" shouted Luke.

55
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:41.187
The speaker on the wall crackled and hissed.

56
00:03:41.188 --> 00:03:44.799
Then Ms. Olson's voice filled the room.

57
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.769
"Students!" the principal reminded them.

58
00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:50.728
"Go immediately to the basement."

59
00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.898
Everyone moved toward the door except Katie.

60
00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:56.523
She was picking up markers.

61
00:03:56.524 --> 00:03:59.970
"Get in line, Katie," Joy said.

62
00:03:59.971 --> 00:04:02.855
"I am," Katie snapped back.

63
00:04:02.856 --> 00:04:06.974
She hated it when Joy told her what to do.

64
00:04:06.975 --> 00:04:09.730
The third graders followed Mr. Higgins.

65
00:04:09.731 --> 00:04:12.882
They went down the stairs to the basement.

66
00:04:12.883 --> 00:04:17.682
Other students entered the basement from all directions.

67
00:04:17.683 --> 00:04:23.822
"Everybody down!" Mr. Higgins called as soon as everyone was standing by the wall.

68
00:04:23.823 --> 00:04:28.450
All the children dropped to the floor in the take-cover position.

69
00:04:28.451 --> 00:04:32.206
Ms. Olson held up her stopwatch and gave it a click.

70
00:04:32.207 --> 00:04:37.485
"Two minutes exactly," she said. "Good work, everyone!"

71
00:04:37.486 --> 00:04:42.838
Back in the classroom, Mr. Higgins passed out a paper to each student.

72
00:04:42.839 --> 00:04:45.721
"We'll finish our posters later.

73
00:04:45.722 --> 00:04:51.875
This is a list of things you can do at home to get ready for tornado season," he said.

74
00:04:51.876 --> 00:04:56.496
"You should each organize a Family Tornado Safety Team."

75
00:04:56.497 --> 00:04:59.858
"Cool," said Luke.

76
00:04:59.859 --> 00:05:04.803
"The Ramirez Tornado Safety Team!" said Carlos.

77
00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:09.846
"The Donovan Tornado Safety Team!" said Katie.

78
00:05:09.847 --> 00:05:15.035
She scribbled something on a piece of notebook paper and then passed it to Joy.

79
00:05:15.036 --> 00:05:23.929
Joy frowned. She could already guess what her sister's note said: I'll be captain!
